=== day
n: 3
title: Lay out the home page
subtitle: Flexbox, Grid and phones
hours: 3 hours
page: index.html
slot: css | css | layout.css
file: layout.css = css
refs: @page, base.css

--- intro
Yesterday you gave a page colours and fonts. Today you decide **where things go**. You build the layout of the ShowShelf **home page**: a top bar, a search bar and a grid of show cards.

The HTML is ready, and so are the colours, fonts and the look of each card: they're in **base.css** (open its tab above the code box to see it). But base.css has no layout at all, so right now everything is stacked in one long column. Your job is **layout.css**.

You'll use three tools that almost every website uses:

- **Flexbox** to put things in a row: the top bar and the search bar
- **Grid** to arrange the cards in columns
- **Media queries** to show more columns on bigger screens

Your colours from Day 2 are already in the page. Open the **index.html (whole page)** tab any time to see the class names you can use.

